> ok i have a problem making the boot disk it formats the disk fine but im not
> gettig a transfer of my autoexec.bat can someone help?


	You may have to create your own.  The following steps are for 
creating a AUTOEXEC.BAT file for arena.

	1: Go into your DOS editor.
	2: Type the following (Type it in as is, DON'T TYPE WHAT IS
	   ENCLOSED IN THE []'S):

	@ECHO OFF
	[SOUND BLASTER ENVIRONMENT SETTINGS, EXAMPLE: SET BLASTER=A220 IXX DX T1]
	PATH=C:\;C:\DOS;C:\[MOUSE DIRECTORY]
	LH MOUSE
	C:
	CD\[FULL DIRECTORY OF GAME DIRECTORY, EXAMPLE: GAMES\ARENA]
	ARENA
	
	3: Make sure that your have loaded your mouse driver by using
	   the LH command before the MOUSE command as above.
	4: After you have typed the above, go to File then to Save.
	5: It will ask you for a file name, type: A:\AUTOEXEC.BAT
	6: This will save it on the A drive and as long as you have
	   your CONFIG.SYS set you are ready to go.
	7: To find your blaster settings, look in your AUTOEXEC.BAT file
	   on your C Drive and that should be in there (this is only assuming
	   that you use a Sound Blaster or compatiable sound card).
	8: For the directory, you have to put in the directory of where the
	   game is at.



